Part 6 run challenge! | Let's run 28k from Vancouver to Lynn Canyon and back (sleep-deprived and underfueled but a full send nonetheless 😆) 

Crossing the 1.3km long Iron Worker’s bridge, not once but TWICE was brutal, and the trail was full of stairs. But the forest, cold dip and the feeling of accomplishment after was so worth it.

So if this is any inspiration and you want to get into running too, don’t stay home on the treadmill this summer! Try planning a destination run that goes somewhere beautiful. It gives you something to chase that isn’t just the mileage! 

Well I'm already excited for next week’s chaos. … care to join us again for the next run? 😉 
______ 
And hey!! if you’re new here, we’re Candace and Geoff, and we’re training for one of the hardest 50K races in the country (#Squamish50), and sharing all the type 2 fun along the way!!

